  "theorem_name": "PrimeSquareDominantThetaLayerDecomposition",
  "declared_proposition": "The exact odd proper-prime-power mass decomposes as W_odd(Y)=theta_odd(floor(sqrt Y))+R_>=3(Y), where R_>=3(Y)=sum_(k>=3)theta_odd(floor(Y^(1/k))). Under the classical Chebyshev bound theta(t)=O(t), R_>=3(Y)=O(Y^(1/3)). Hence the Goldbach contamination envelope has a prime-square leading term 2 log(N) theta_odd(floor(sqrt N)) plus O(N^(1/3) log N) and the exact power-of-two term. Higher layers cannot be deleted exactly: 32=27+5 is a cube-prime contamination witness.",
  "mathematical_argument": "Separate k=2 in the exact TICKET-194 theta identity. Chebyshev bounds the k=3 layer by O(Y^(1/3)); every k>=4 layer is O(Y^(1/4)), and O(log Y)Y^(1/4)=O(Y^(1/3)). Multiplication by the partner log weight yields the stated remainder.",
